# CCCL → hipCUB Sync: <CURRENT_TAG> → <TO_TAG> — TODO

We are in the middle of a manual-port sync of upstream CCCL/CUB commits
into hipCUB. There is no git merge in progress and never will be — this
sync is a series of hand-ported commits, one local commit per item below,
audited at the end by `hipcub-cccl-sync-finalize`. This file tracks which
upstream commits still need to be ported.

## Sync parameters

- **JIRA ticket**: <JIRA_TICKET> (if any — no fixed project exists for
  hipCUB syncs)
- **Repo**: `ROCm/rocm-libraries` — hipCUB lives at `projects/hipccl/hipccl3/hipcub/`
- **Sync base branch** (`$SYNC_BASE`): <SYNC_BASE>
- **Confirmed current tag** (`$CURRENT_TAG`): <CURRENT_TAG>
- **Target tag** (`$TO_TAG`): <TO_TAG>
- **Sync branch** (`$SYNC_BRANCH`, currently checked out): <SYNC_BRANCH>
- **Investigation report**: <INVESTIGATION_REPORT_PATH_OR_NONE>
- **Path reminder**: hipCUB is a wrapper, not a copy. An upstream public
  header `cub/cub/<dir>/<name>.cuh` corresponds to up to three hipCUB
  headers under `projects/hipccl/hipccl3/hipcub/hipcub/include/hipcub/`:
  `<dir>/<name>.hpp` (platform forwarder), `backend/rocprim/<dir>/<name>.hpp`
  (implemented on rocPRIM) and `backend/cub/<dir>/<name>.hpp` (wraps CUB;
  block/warp and many thread/iterator headers have no file here because
  `backend/cub/hipcub.hpp` re-exports them). Upstream
  `cub/cub/{device/dispatch,agent,detail}/` have no hipCUB copy.
  Tests: `cub/test/catch2_test_<x>.cu` → `projects/hipccl/hipccl3/hipcub/test/hipcub/test_hipcub_<x>.cpp`
  (Google Test). Benchmarks: `cub/benchmarks/bench/<algo>/` →
  `projects/hipccl/hipccl3/hipcub/benchmark/benchmark_device_<algo>.cpp`. Examples:
  `cub/examples/<sub>/` → `projects/hipccl/hipccl3/hipcub/examples/<sub>/`.

## ⚠ Ordering rule

Commits below are listed **strictly oldest-first**. Only the first unticked
(`- [ ]`) item may be worked next. Do not skip ahead, reorder, or batch
multiple commits together — a later commit may assume an earlier one is
already applied (it may reference symbols the earlier commit introduces, or
fix a bug the earlier commit itself introduced).

## State of the sync

- No `git merge` is in progress. There is no `MERGE_HEAD`, and no conflict
  markers will ever appear as part of this process.
- Ticked (`- [X]`) items below are **committed** on the sync branch: one
  local commit per item, including N/A items (empty commit), whose subject
  contains `port CCCL <sha11>`. The tick-note records it as `Local commit:
  <sha>`.
- This file itself is untracked and is never committed. Nothing is pushed
  until the human decides to. Avoid `git reset --hard` on this branch.
- `CCCL_MINIMUM_VERSION` (`cmake/Dependencies.cmake`),
  `HIPCUB_CCCL_VERSION_*` (`CMakeLists.txt`) and `CHANGELOG.md` are not
  touched by any item; the human bumps them separately.

